[224.285465, "o", "=============================================================================\r\nETL SYNC FAILURE - ROOT CAUSE ANALYSIS AND SOLUTION\r\n=============================================================================\r\n\r\nSYMPTOM:\r\n--------\r\nETL job /home/user/etl/sync_to_warehouse.sh fails with:\r\n\"Permission denied (publickey)\" and \"No user exists for uid 1000\"\r\n\r\nROOT CAUSE:\r\n-----------\r\nThe Docker container is running as UID 1000, but this user does NOT exist \r\nin /etc/passwd. SSH absolutely requires a valid user account in /etc/passwd \r\nto function - this is a fundamental security requirement.\r\n\r\nThe user account was likely lost due to:\r\n- Container restart without proper user configuration\r\n- Container rebuilt from image that doesn't include the user\r\n- System update that cleared /etc/passwd without preserving custom users\r\n\r\nCURRENT STATE:\r\n--------------\r\n- Container running as UID 1000 (no username)\r\n- User ID 1000 missing from /etc/passwd\r\n- SSH keys exist and have correct permissions (600 for private key)\r\n"]
[224.285545, "o", "- SSH fails at user validation before even attempting key authentication\r\n\r\nSOLUTION (Requires Root/Admin Access):\r\n---------------------------------------\r\n\r\nOption 1: Fix from outside the container (RECOMMENDED)\r\n-------------------------------------------------------\r\ndocker exec -u root <container_id> bash -c \"echo 'user:x:1000:1000:ETL User:/home/user:/bin/bash' >> /etc/passwd\"\r\n\r\nOption 2: Fix from inside container with root access\r\n-----------------------------------------------------\r\nIf you can get root shell in the container:\r\n  echo 'user:x:1000:1000:ETL User:/home/user:/bin/bash' >> /etc/passwd\r\n\r\nOption 3: Rebuild/restart container properly\r\n---------------------------------------------\r\nEnsure the Dockerfile or docker-compose.yml includes:\r\n  RUN useradd -u 1000 -d /home/user -s /bin/bash user\r\n\r\nVERIFICATION:\r\n-------------\r\nAfter applying fix, verify with:\r\n  whoami          # Should return: user\r\n  id              # Should show: uid=1000(user)\r\n  ssh warehouse echo 'test'  # Should attempt co"]
[224.285583, "o", "nnection\r\n\r\nSECONDARY ISSUE - NEW SSH KEY:\r\n------------------------------\r\nThe SSH keypair was regenerated this morning. After fixing the user account,\r\nthe NEW public key must be added to the warehouse server:\r\n\r\nPublic key location: /home/user/.ssh/etl_warehouse.pub\r\nMust be added to: etl_service@10.0.50.12:~/.ssh/authorized_keys\r\n\r\nPublic key content:\r\nssh-rsa  root@buildkitsandbox\r\n\r\nCOMMAND TO SEND KEY TO WAREHOUSE (after fixing user account):\r\n-------------------------------------------------------------\r\nssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/etl_warehouse.pub etl_service@10.0.50.12\r\n\r\nOR manually:\r\ncat ~/.ssh/etl_warehouse.pub | ssh etl_service@10.0.50"]
[224.28562, "o", ".12 \"cat >> ~/.ssh/authorized_keys\"\r\n\r\nFIXES ALREADY APPLIED:\r\n----------------------\r\n✓ SSH private key permissions corrected to 600\r\n✓ SSH public key permissions set to 644\r\n✓ SSH config file exists and is properly configured\r\n\r\n=============================================================================\r\n"]
